#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083086 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "367fe9fb-9d92-5105-9959-f3861994aa3c" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Repeating Decimal as an Infinite Geometric Series"}] :question/id #uuid "acebcd95-16ed-5087-8d04-0d6d503e31f3" :question/math-academy-id "e-694" :question/problem "Write $0.\\overline{23}$ as geometric series." :question/worked-solution "The given repeating decimal can be written as\n\n$$\n0.\\overline{23} = 0.23 + 0.002\\,3 + 0.000\\,023 + \\dots\n$$\n\n$$\n0.\\overline{23} = \\dfrac{23}{100} + \\dfrac{23}{10\\,000} + \\dfrac{23}{1\\,000\\,000}+\\dots\n$$\n\nwhere the first term is\n\n$$\na_1 = \\dfrac{23}{100}\n$$\n\nand the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{100}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0.23^(―) &= ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)a_{1}r^{n - 1} \\\\\n&= ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)\\frac{23}{100} \\cdot (\\frac{1}{100})^{n - 1} \\\\\n&= ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)23 \\cdot \\frac{1}{100} \\cdot (\\frac{1}{100})^{n - 1} \\\\\n&= ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)23 \\cdot \\frac{1}{100} \\cdot (\\frac{1}{100})^{n} \\cdot (\\frac{1}{100})^{-1} \\\\\n&= ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)23(\\frac{1}{100})^{n}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083087 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083285 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8813b8a0-3b5e-5cd8-a37d-6b921f2882b8" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Repeating Decimal as the Sum of a Number and a Geometric Series"}] :question/id #uuid "ed24fd0c-69c1-502a-a05f-6e859724214a" :question/math-academy-id "e-695" :question/problem "Write $0.1\\overline{4}$ as geometric series." :question/worked-solution "The given repeating decimal can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0.14^(―) &= 0.1444... \\\\\n&= 0.1 + 0.04 + 0.004 + 0.0004 + … \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10} + (\\frac{4}{100} + \\frac{4}{1000} + \\frac{4}{10000} + …)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe series in the parentheses is a geometric series with the first term\n\n$$\na_1 = \\dfrac{4}{100}\n$$\n\nand the common ratio\n\n$$\nr=\\dfrac{1}{10}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0.14^(―) &= \\frac{1}{10} + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)a_{1}r^{n - 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10} + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)\\frac{4}{100}(\\frac{1}{10})^{n - 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10} + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)\\frac{4 \\cdot 10}{100}(\\frac{1}{10})^{n} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10} + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)\\frac{4}{10}(\\frac{1}{10})^{n}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083691 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083285 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8813b8a0-3b5e-5cd8-a37d-6b921f2882b8" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Repeating Decimal as the Sum of a Number and a Geometric Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "803467b1-2020-5624-a5ad-19640860beed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7 + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)\\frac{8}{9}(\\frac{1}{10})^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081078} {:answer/id #uuid "c2818ad8-51ea-5375-b9df-40101f92ab9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.8 + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)\\frac{7}{10}(\\frac{1}{10})^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081079} {:answer/id #uuid "ef6d241d-38e7-550f-8a38-abc833ff722d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.8 + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)\\frac{8}{10}(\\frac{1}{10})^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081080} {:answer/id #uuid "0fe3b103-34c1-50b3-88e4-db64f9c0f245" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.8 + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)\\frac{7}{10}(\\frac{1}{100})^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081081} {:answer/id #uuid "10e59e9c-64bc-5792-9a7c-3a893db2ef41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.8 + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)\\frac{7}{100}(\\frac{1}{100})^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081082}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7ef4297c-0c05-56d2-a418-f8b435501b80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ide